INT. ABANDONED BOARDING SCHOOL - DORMITORY WING - NIGHT

A long room of iron cots, each with a stained mattress. Peeling wallpaper patterned with faded violets. A cracked mirror at the end of the room. Moonlight through ragged curtains. The air is thick with damp.

PROFESSOR LORETTA ACHEBE-VANCE, 50s, tweed jacket, notebook, steps through the door with a lantern held high. She is a historian, and she is tired. Behind her, her graduate student THADDEUS NWOKE-BRIGGS, 20s, narrow shoulders, backpack too large. And behind him, a ghost-tour guide from the village, MRS. PRUDENCE OYELOWO, 60s, in a brown cardigan, clutching rosary beads.

LORETTA
Cots numbered, but not in order.

THADDEUS
Fourteen. Nine. Twenty-two.

LORETTA
And this one?

She stops beside a cot. Its pillow bears a deep hollow. A child's shape pressed in.

MRS. PRUDENCE
(whispering)
Don't touch that one.

LORETTA
Why not?

MRS. PRUDENCE
That was Eleanor's.

THADDEUS
Eleanor who?

MRS. PRUDENCE
The girl who stopped sleeping.

Thaddeus laughs, nervously, then stops. Loretta sets the lantern on the cot's frame and kneels. The flame shivers.

LORETTA
(low)
This mattress is warm.

THADDEUS
That's impossible.

LORETTA
Feel it.

He hesitates. Crosses. Lays two fingers on the sheet. Pulls them back.

THADDEUS
It is.

MRS. PRUDENCE
Out. All of you. Now.

LORETTA
Mrs. Oyelowo --

MRS. PRUDENCE
She doesn't like people who stay.

At the far end of the dormitory, the cracked mirror gives a small, metallic tick. All three turn. In its dark glass, a faint figure stands at the end of a bed. A girl in a long nightgown, head tilted, hands folded.

LORETTA
(whispering)
Nobody move.

THADDEUS
That's not a reflection. There's nobody there.

MRS. PRUDENCE
(rosary clicking)
Hail Mary, full of grace...

The girl in the mirror lifts her head. Her face is blank, a pale oval without features. She raises a hand and points directly at Thaddeus.

THADDEUS
Why me?

LORETTA
Back away. Slowly.

He backs. His heel catches on a cot leg. The iron frame scrapes the floor with a shriek. The mirror shatters, shards falling in a silver rain.

The lantern gutters. The dormitory plunges into darkness. Somewhere in the black, the creak of a hundred cots shifting under unseen weight.

MRS. PRUDENCE (CONT'D)
(screaming)
Run!

They do. Boots clatter on the floorboards. The lantern rolls and goes out.

INT. DORMITORY CORRIDOR - CONTINUOUS

They tumble through the door and into the corridor, gasping. Loretta slams it shut. A heavy thud answers from the other side.

LORETTA
Hold it!

Thaddeus throws his shoulder against the door. Mrs. Prudence presses her back against it. The thuds come faster. Harder. Something laughs, high and child-like.

THADDEUS
It's strong!

LORETTA
It's a child!

MRS. PRUDENCE
It's not a child anymore!

The door bulges. Loretta digs in her satchel, pulls out a brass key.

LORETTA
There's a lock!

THADDEUS
Do it!

She rams the key in, turns. The bolt clunks home. The thudding stops. In the silence, they sink to the floor, panting.

A tiny voice speaks from beneath the door. Barely a whisper.

ELEANOR (O.S.)
Don't leave me.

None of them answer.
